aaca4068df: pending cleared, one proposal waiting). Where the owner is gone, no replica can complete the operation, because a proposal is never transmitted: handlePropose attaches the GPropose to the instance's local bookkeeping and recovery preserves only the recovering replica's own record's proposals, so the operation exists in no surviving process; the captured driver client sends each proposal once and then blocks on the reply stream with no timeout or retry, so nothing re-issues it either (S13-handleCommit, S8-handlePropose-startPhase1, S28-client-waitreplies, S29-client-sendproposal). The absence of an in-repository mechanism is therefore a contract boundary rather than an unnoticed replica bug: completion after the admitting replica is lost is owed to a client retry that this snapshot does not implement.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"whether the audited contract includes the test driver's retry behaviour, which decides whether this boundary is a defect of the implementation or an external obligation\\\",\n   \\\"whether a client retry would be safe here, since no duplicate suppression exists and the replica's own TODO still lists client retries as unhandled\\\",\n   \\\"the open scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact, and the unread surfaces (replica/sender.go, replica/mset.go, hook/, master/)\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Pausing rather than explaining: one half is now a confirmed protection (C5) and the other half is a design boundary that no in-repository mechanism covers, which is a contract question rather than an implemented mechanism. The pause conditions name exactly what would reopen it, and the candidate's basis is preserved with its refined unknowns.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{\\\"b7160e779313408b8d1f7e88b35e71c5\\\":upd}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"pause\\\",\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"b7160e779313408b8d1f7e88b35e71c5\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Pauses the client-completion Candidate with its two halves answered: the owner-alive half is a confirmed protection (claim C5) and the owner-gone half is a contract boundary in which no replica can complete the operation because proposals are never transmitted, while the driver client neither retries nor times out. What would reopen it is a client retry implementation, a replica-side proposal transfer, or a harness that drives the client library.\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":q,\\\"resume_conditions\\\":rc,\\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-pause-client.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-pause-client.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
