{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-pause-client.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 39 closed the client-completion question by pausing the Candidate with both halves sourced and explicit resume conditions.\\n\\nWhat was decided. The owner-alive half is a confirmed protection: the reviewed check for claim C5 showed that an owner which still holds the admitted operation installs the single-NONE commit and re-proposes the operation onto the propose channel (artifact fb1d0e558f4641c7850fe8aaca4068df, pending cleared, one proposal waiting). The owner-gone half is a contract boundary rather than an unnoticed replica bug: a proposal is never transmitted — handlePropose attaches it to the instance's local bookkeeping and recovery preserves only the recovering replica's own record's proposals — so no surviving process holds the operation, and the captured driver client sends each proposal once and then blocks on the reply stream with no timeout or retry. Completion after the admitting replica is lost is therefore owed to a client retry that this snapshot does not implement, and the replica's own TODO still lists client retries as unhandled.\\n\\nProduct. The Candidate is paused on its stored proposition with resume conditions naming exactly what would reopen it: a client-side retry implementation, a replica-side mechanism that transfers an admitted proposal when leadership of its instance changes, or a harness that drives the client library against the replica harness so the missing reply can be observed end to end. Its unknowns are refined to the two open questions (whether the replica implementation is expected to complete another replica's proposal, and whether the driver client's retry behaviour is inside the audited contract), and the feedback cites C5, the proposal-handling and client sources, and the client read as the evidence.\\n\\nFrontier. Audit spec version 7; five claims are settled (C1 recovery divergence, C2 stable-store record, C3 applied-state divergence, C4 the NOOP-commit crash, C5 the owner-alive re-proposal protection); the accept-status candidate remains paused with its resume conditions; the remaining visible debts are the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact and the unread surfaces (replica/sender.go, replica/mset.go, hook/, master/). No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
